<h2>What we use</h2>
<p>All the cookies and data stored in your browser that QR Menu uses are technical or store a preference you choose. They don't require your consent, which is why we don't show a cookie banner.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Session (<code>PHPSESSID</code>):</strong> keeps you signed in to the panel while you use it. It is deleted when you close the browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep me signed in (<code>REMEMBERME</code>):</strong> only if you tick "Keep me signed in" when signing in; saves you from signing in again for 7 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Form security (<code>csrf-token</code>):</strong> protects forms against forged submissions. It lasts as long as the session.</li>
    <li><strong>Language of these pages (<code>site_lang</code>):</strong> remembers the language you pick with the selector, for one year. Only created if you change the language.</li>
    <li><strong>Menu preferences (<code>menu_prefs</code>):</strong> remembers the language and currency you pick when viewing a restaurant's menu, for one year.</li>
    <li><strong>Light or dark mode (<code>admin-theme</code>, <code>site-theme</code>):</strong> stored in your browser's local storage (not cookies) to remember how you prefer to see the panel and these pages.</li>
    <li><strong>Conversation with the virtual waiter (<code>sw_conv_…</code>):</strong> stored in the tab's storage (not a cookie) to continue the conversation; deleted when you close the tab.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What we don't use</h2>
<p>We don't use advertising, analytics or tracking cookies, neither our own nor third-party ones. Fonts and icons are served from our own server.</p>

<h2>How to manage them</h2>
<p>You can delete or block cookies and local storage in your browser settings. If you block the session cookie, you won't be able to sign in to the panel.</p>

<p>For more information on how we process your data, see our <a href="{{ path('app_privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
